---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const title = 'Affiliate disclosure';
const description = 'How Mailbox Atlas may earn money from links to virtual mailbox providers, and which links are affiliate links.';
---
<Base title={title} description={description} updated="2026-11-25">
  <h1>Affiliate disclosure</h1>
  <p><strong>Current status (November 25, 2026):</strong> we have affiliate relationships with US Global Mail, Virtual Post Mail, Traveling Mailbox, BlueNotary and Notarize. Links to those providers may earn us a commission, at no extra cost to you. Every other provider link still goes to that provider's public website, and we earn nothing from it.</p>
  <p>Active affiliate programs:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>US Global Mail, since November 21, 2026</li>
    <li>Virtual Post Mail, since November 21, 2026</li>
    <li>Traveling Mailbox, since November 25, 2026</li>
    <li>BlueNotary, since November 21, 2026</li>
    <li>Notarize, since November 21, 2026</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We may apply to affiliate programs run by other providers we cover, such as iPostal1, Anytime Mailbox and PostScan Mail. If one approves us, links to that provider may become affiliate links, and the provider may pay us a commission at no extra cost to you. We'll list each one here with the date.</p>
  <p>Active affiliate links are marked <span class="aff-tag">affiliate link</span> and carry <code>rel="sponsored"</code>. Other provider links are ordinary links; they are not marked, and we earn nothing from them until a program is listed above.</p>
  <h2>Our rules</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Commissions never change a price, a fact, or the order of a table.</li>
    <li>If a commission-paying provider is the more expensive choice for a situation, we say so.</li>
    <li>We include providers that don't pay us whenever leaving them out would make a comparison worse.</li>
  </ul>
</Base>
